---

# What Concatenation Means

Concatenation means:

```text id="xmlns228"
joining strings together
```

Example:

```ruby id="xmlns229"
first_name + " " + last_name
```

Ruby combines them into one string.

---

# What Interpolation Means

Interpolation means:

```text id="xmlns230"
inserting variables directly inside a string
```

Example:

```ruby id="xmlns231"
"#{first_name} #{last_name}"
```

Ruby replaces the placeholders with actual values.

