# Important Correction

In Ruby:

```ruby id="xmlns247"
==
```

is the standard equality operator.

You used:

```ruby id="xmlns248"
===
```

It works in some cases, but usually for beginner Ruby logic you should use:

```ruby id="xmlns249"
==
```

Example:

```ruby id="xmlns250"
if input == "marco"
```

Cleaner and more standard.

